{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqbftisxmkr","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"harness adapter architecture: daemon core plus MCP stays portable, Claude adapter preserved unchanged","summary":"DECISION: split Zonoid into a harness-agnostic core (daemon, routes, overlay, graph store, context gate, judge, MCP surface) and per-harness adapters behind a single interface. The existing Claude Code integration becomes the first adapter and its behavior is preserved EXACTLY as-is (user requirement): native task files under ~/.claude/tasks via lib/native-tasks.js, transcript parsing under ~/.claude/projects via lib/human-input.js, scheduled-task follow-ups via lib/followups.js, and the hooks/ scripts stay at their current paths because installed settings.json files reference them. Adapter seam = task source (aggregate, read, write status, watch, format health), transcript or usage source, and scheduler. Later adapters: Cursor, Codex, OpenCode; a daemon-native task source plus create_task MCP tool will make any MCP-capable harness usable without reverse-engineering its internals. Work happens on branch feat/harness-adapters in a worktree, phase 1 is a pure seam extraction with zero behavior change and the full test suite green.","created_by":null,"valid_from":"2026-06-12T21:27:30.417Z","vec":[-0.09410843998193741,-0.037738826125860214,0.014304099604487419,0.01522394735366106,0.09140640497207642,0.034243274480104446,-0.043566200882196426,0.03512028232216835,-0.06239166483283043,-0.0025018395390361547,0.0820445567369461,0.02154099941253662,0.017999183386564255,0.017899205908179283,-0.04809148237109184,0.01776435226202011,0.01778608374297619,0.010523688048124313,0.06916496157646179,-0.025647802278399467,-0.06662800908088684,-0.04694478586316109,-0.06598450988531113,0.03433801606297493,-0.03864683955907822,-0.040238648653030396,0.031450629234313965,-0.0418071448802948,-0.04144987836480141,-0.033284176141023636,0.014262104406952858,-0.03419823572039604,-0.07954780